# Modules

`Session` constructs match widgets and subscribes (`onLookAt`, `onKind`, …). It never grabs a child canvas or implements that widget's pointer machine.

`Session` exists only while a match is running, inside `PlayScreen`. `ScreenHost` shows exactly one `GameScreen`. `play(mapId)` shows a `PlayScreen`; Exit (confirm) replaces it.

```
app/      Pixi boot, ScreenHost, ticker. Creates Session on demand. Constructs Channel.
session/  One match: that map, input, widget subscriptions. Talks to Lockstep, never a socket.
sim/      Deterministic world. No Pixi, fetch, DOM, or net.
render/   Pixi drawing. Reads views, does not mutate sim.
ui/       DOM widgets and GameScreens. Own their DOM and input.
net/      Channel + lockstep mailbox. No Pixi, no rules, no World.tick.
```

```ts
// BAD — session reaches into the widget
hud.minimap.addEventListener("pointerdown", ...)
paintMinimap(hud.minimap, view)

// GOOD
new Minimap(host, { onLookAt: (x, y) => session.lookAt(x, y) })
minimap.setView(view)
```
